{"record": "turn", "turn": 4, "seconds": 6.305, "response_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "stop_reason": "tool_use", "stop_details": null, "blocks": ["thinking", "tool_use"], "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 10935, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 947, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "tools": [{"id": "toolu_01FqKERwMmcFcfwZZKGCwPhz", "name": "submit_answer", "arguments": {"answer": "No. The dSph analysis (Sec. 4.2) sets the one-sided 95% upper limit where 2Δln L = 2.71 (a drop of 2.71 in TS, or 1.355 in ln L), and it profiles over each dwarf's J-factor, using a Gaussian prior on log10 s with width σ_J and range log10 s in [-3, 3]. The AMS-02 antiproton analysis (Sec. 5) takes the upper endpoint of the ΔQ ≤ 3.84 region, where Q = -2 ln L, which is the nominal two-sided 95% threshold for one parameter of interest. The paper says this differs from the one-sided 2.71 prescription. It profiles over the Galactic diffusive-halo half-height L, using a Gaussian penalty in log10 L centred at 4.96 kpc with σ = 0.197, over 1 ≤ L/kpc ≤ 12.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.2"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "5"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.3"}]}, "status": "answer", "error_kind": null, "seconds": 0.0}]}
{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261120T075229Z_dev-02_staged_15b7", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "No. The dSph analysis (Sec. 4.2) sets the one-sided 95% upper limit where 2Δln L = 2.71 (a drop of 2.71 in TS, or 1.355 in ln L), and it profiles over each dwarf's J-factor, using a Gaussian prior on log10 s with width σ_J and range log10 s in [-3, 3]. The AMS-02 antiproton analysis (Sec. 5) takes the upper endpoint of the ΔQ ≤ 3.84 region, where Q = -2 ln L, which is the nominal two-sided 95% threshold for one parameter of interest. The paper says this differs from the one-sided 2.71 prescription. It profiles over the Galactic diffusive-halo half-height L, using a Gaussian penalty in log10 L centred at 4.96 kpc with σ = 0.197, over 1 ≤ L/kpc ≤ 12.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.2"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "5"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.3"}]}, "turns": 4, "seconds": 10.888, "tool_calls": 4, "tool_result_chars": 19377, "input_tokens": 10, "output_tokens": 1266, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 25366, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-20T07:52:40+00:00"}
